d the cutpoints, `method = :probit_liability`). The BINARY (`:bernoulli_probit`) observed-0/1 scale is computed via the QGglmm probit integration over `η~N(μ,V_A+V_fixed)` (`Ψ²V_A/[p̄(1−p̄)]`) — verified EQUAL to the Dempster–Lerner `z²/[p(1−p)]` and `< h²_liab`; the ORDINAL (K>2) per-category observed scale is now computed as the VECTOR `h2_observation_by_category` (`h²_k = Ψ_k²V_A/[p_k(1−p_k)]` per category indicator, over `η~N(μ,V_A+V_fixed)`; the scalar `h2_observation` stays NaN), VALIDATED to ≤3e-8 vs QGglmm `model=ordinal` (`comparator/qgglmm_ordinal_observed/`). Validated (`test/runtests.jl`): the ordinal per-category vector incl. the K=2→binary-observed reduction; the Gaussian reduction; the `_trigamma` closed forms (ψ₁(1)=π²/6, ψ₁(2)=π²/6−1, ψ₁(½)=π²/2) + recurrence + the Gamma latent closed form (μ-independent, V_fixed denominator, monotone-in-ν, shape guards); the probit/ordinal liability closed form incl. the exact K=2 ordinal→bernoulli-probit reduction + the V_fixed denominator; the binary observed = Dempster–Lerner cross-check (≈1e-6, obs < liab); the logit latent closed form; the logit observation-scale anchored against an INDEPENDENT 64-node quadrature of the same integrals (rtol 1e-3, 0<h²_obs<1); the Poisson degeneracy + closed form vs independent integration (rtol 1e-6); the Binomial n_trials information gradient (h²_obs rises 1→5→20); and guards (refuses a non-converged fit; per-record varying n_trials → NaN+caveat; ambiguous μ on a multi-β fit throws; Bernoulli information_limited = true; unsupported families throw). Dependency-free (reuses the 20-node GH). NOT added to `nongaussian_result_payload`. Still needs — a same-estimand external comparator: QGglmm RUN + AGREES (≤4.5e-6, 25 comparisons) for the logit + binary-probit + Poisson(count) + Binomial(n>1) observation scales (all four QGglmm builtins; `comparator/qgglmm_probit_observed/`; doc-19 §5), the ordinal-K>2 observed comparator is now RUN + AGREES (≤3e-8 via QGglmm `model=ordinal`), and