 | V6-GGLLVM-DESC | Genetic-GLLVM latent-structure descriptors + Gaussian latent solve (supplied loadings) (Phase 6, #50 slices 1–2) | partial | `genetic_gllvm_descriptors(Λ; uniqueness)` reports the rotation-INVARIANT descriptors of a genetic-GLLVM latent layer from SUPPLIED `traits × K` loadings `Λ` (+ optional positive uniqueness `Ψ`): `genetic_covariance` `Σ_g = ΛΛ' (+ diag Ψ)`, `genetic_variances`, `genetic_correlation`, `communality` `c²_t = (ΛΛ')_tt / Σ_g[t,t]`, `genetic_pca`/`g_max`, and `rank`/`n_latent_factors = K` — a pure composition of `lowrank_covariance`/`factor_analytic_covariance`/`genetic_correlation` (`multivariate.jl`) and `genetic_pca`/`g_max` (`evolvability.jl`), no new estimation. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`, 24 deterministic RNG-free assertions): exact `Σ_g == lowrank_covariance(Λ)` (Ψ absent) and `== factor_analytic_covariance(Λ, Ψ)`; `communality == 1` at `Ψ = 0`, matches `(ΛΛ')_tt / Σ_g[t,t]` and is strictly in `(0,1)` with positive `Ψ`; the binding rotation-invariance gate (for orthogonal `Q`, `Λ → ΛQ` leaves `Σ_g`, `genetic_variances`, `communality`, `genetic_correlation`, and the `genetic_pca` eigenvalues invariant); the `K = t`, `Λ = I`, `Ψ = 0` reduction (`Σ_g = I`, communality 1, eigenvalues all 1); and delegated dimension/positivity/rank guards. DESCRIPTIVE, supplied-covariance only — `Λ`/`Ψ` NOT estimated, no marginal/likelihood/fit, no R model-spec or bridge payload, only rotation-invariant functionals (never raw loadings). Slice 2 adds the Gaussian latent solve `genetic_gllvm_gaussian_mme(Y, X, Z, Ainv, Λ, R0; uniqueness)`: since `Cov(vec(U)) = G_lat ⊗ A` under a Gaussian response, the Gaussian genetic GLLVM IS the multivariate animal model at `G0 = G_lat = ΛΛ'(+diag Ψ)`, so the function builds `G_lat` and delegates to `multivariate_mme`, returning that solve plus the rotation-invariant `latent_structure`. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`): the defining identity (`== multivariate_mme` at `G0 = G_lat`, exact β + EBVs), rotation invariance of β/EBVs under `Λ → ΛQ`, the `t = 1, K = 1` reduction to the univariate `henderson_mme`, and guards (trait-count mismatch; a singular pure-low-rank `G_lat` with `K < t` and no `Ψ` rejected — `G_lat` must be PD). The solve's numerical correctness reduces to `multivariate_mme` (V4-MV); `Λ`/`Ψ`/`R0` are NOT estimated (slice 3). An overload `genetic_gllvm_descriptors(result)` reports the same rotation-invariant descriptors for an ESTIMATED `:factor_analytic`/`:lowrank` multivariate REML fit from its estimated `G` and reported `Ψ` (separate Ψ identification depends on the loading pattern; never raw loadings), `communality = 1 − Ψ/diag(G)`, validated against the real deterministic `fa`/`low` fixture fits plus a synthetic structured result and rejecting the rotation-free `:diagonal`/`:unstructured` structures (`test/runtests.jl`). Still needs mixed-family and broader-design recovery, unbalanced/missing-record support, and external same-objective GLLVM.jl/gllvmTMB comparator parity |
