gument also accepts a length-`T` `Vector` of `ResponseFamily` (per-trait families) as well as a single scalar family — a uniform vector equals the scalar path EXACTLY, mixed Poisson+Gaussian traits converge, and a wrong-length vector is guarded (`test/runtests.jl`, 8 assertions). Experimental, dense/validation-scale, SUPPLIED loadings (NOT estimated), per-trait or shared families, balanced/fully-observed `Y`, INTERNAL (not exported). Still needs mixed-family known-truth recovery, unbalanced/missing-record support, and external same-objective GLLVM.jl/gllvmTMB comparator parity (genetic-GLLVM Laplace-marginal fitting over this marginal — slice 3 — now exists, see `V6-GGLLVM-LAPLACE`) |
 | V6-GGLLVM-LAPLACE | Genetic-GLLVM integrated-Laplace fitting — estimate the latent G_lat (Phase 6, #50 slice 3) | partial | `fit_gllvm_laplace_reml(Y, Ainv, family; rank, X)` (internal) ESTIMATES the rank-`K` latent loadings `Λ` (`G_lat = ΛΛ'`) by maximizing the K-factor fixed-and-genetic-effect integrated Laplace objective (`gllvm_laplace_marginal_loglik`) over `vec(Λ)` (NelderMead). The marginal depends on `Λ` only through `G_lat = ΛΛ'`, so it is rotation-invariant; the result reports the rotation-INVARIANT `genetic_covariance` / `latent_structure` (never the raw `Λ̂`, an arbitrary point on the rotation manifold). Validated (`test/runtests.jl`): the `K=1, T=1` Poisson case reduces to the single-factor `fit_laplace_reml` (`σ²a = λ̂²`, rtol 2e-3); a multi-trait Poisson rank-1 fit converges and its optimum improves over the start (objective maximized); and the Gaussian optimum's marginal equals `_multivariate_reml_loglik` at the estimated `Λ̂Λ̂'` (`R0 = σ²e·I`, rtol 1e-7) — self-consistency of the reported `G_lat`. A `structure = :factor_analytic` option additionally estimates a per-trait specific genetic variance `Ψ > 0` (`G_lat = ΛΛ' + diag(Ψ)`, on the `log` scale, by augmenting the loadings to `[Λ | diag(√Ψ)]` and reusing the marginal unchanged); validated by the Gaussian self-consistency at `Ĝ = Λ̂Λ̂'+Ψ̂`, `communality < 1` (since `Ψ̂ > 0`), `FA loglik ≥ low-rank loglik` (FA nests low-rank), a converging Poisson FA fit, and length/structure guards. For `GaussianResponse(σ²e)` the scalar residual `σ²e` is FIXED (not estimated); the non-Gaussian families have no residual. A correctness-validated ESTIMATOR (reductions + optimum-improvement + Gaussian self-consistency). An opt-in known-truth recovery harness (`sim/phase6_gllvm_recovery.jl`, outside CI; checkpoint `docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-06-20-genetic-gllvm-reml-recovery.md`) now records FOUR scenarios across THREE families: (A) Poisson rank-1 (`Λ=[1.0,0.7,0.5]`, `q=240`): 5/5 seeds, mean rel `0.091`; (B) Poisson rank-2 NON-degenerate-ρ (`q=120`): 5/5, mean rel `0.205`, genetic correlations `mean|Δρ|=0.089`; (C) Bernoulli rank-1 logit (`Λ=[0.9,0.6,0.4]`, `q=240`, `μ=0`): REPORTED-NOT-GATED — mean rel `0.540`, 3/5 below threshold, one seed rel `1.15` — the observed unsigned relative error on the latent `G_lat` scale; five seeds do not establish bias direction or cause; (D) Binomial(20) rank-1 logit (same DGP, `m=20` trials): 5/5, mean rel `0.104` — a descriptive five-seed contrast that does not establish an information-quantity cause. All 20 fits across all four scenarios converged. **Consumability additions (2026-06-20):** `family` now accepts a length-`T` `Vector{ResponseFamily}` (per-trait families) — threaded through to `gllvm_laplace_marginal_loglik` (which already supported them) by widening the historical fitter signature from `ResponseFamily` to `Union{ResponseFamily, AbstractVector}`; a uniform vector gives numerically identical objectives to the scalar path (same optimizer path, exact `genetic_covariance` equality on the 8-animal Poisson rank-1 fixture). `fit_gllvm_laplace_reml` now returns a typed **`GeneticGLLVMFit`** struct (internal, not exported) instead of a bare `NamedTuple`, with typed extractors `genetic_covariance(fit)`, `breeding_values(fit)` (`q×T` trait genetic conditional modes, including FA-specific modes), `latent_structure(fit)`, and `loglik(fit)` dispatching on the concrete struct type — not on `NamedTuple`, so no collision with the multivariate extractors; field access `fit.fieldname` continues to work unchanged. All 21 prior REML testset assertions pass with the new return type; 19 new consumability assertions added (testset "Genetic-GLLVM consumability"). A separate frozen 50-seed ordinary-start Poisson `T=3, K=2` replay was rerun against the pinned current fitter source and passed 50/50; it reuses the 50 seeds from the September ordinary-start primary run and is one-cell reproducibility/usability evidence, not an independent 100-